sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task + full intent as inputs, single-swamp-node; DECISIONS 4 / R1-R4 (process.stop shape), round 2 (admit instead of refuse; php_input and runtime_definitions as inputs), 3 (rollback removes the auto-deploy schedule); rule 7 (reload over restart, restart_on_deploy only). docs/reference/deployments.md#roll-back.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:rollback
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-prod Node<br/>Node 12 over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:rollback 42<br/>--release=20261030T101500Z
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:rollback 42 --release=20261030T101500Z`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> --release=NAME [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance, and one retained release name from `instance:release:list 42`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Check release, admit<br/>Instance 42 locked · task #5151
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Instance 42 is a production Instance; else `deployment_config.unavailable`
  %%> - Instance 42 retains release `20261030T101500Z`; else `rollback.release_not_retained` and nothing changes
  %%> - no started operation holds Instance 42; else `operation.target_busy`
  %%> Wins over:
  %%> - a deploy that no worker has started; it ends `cancelled` with `operation.superseded`
  %%> Freezes:
  %%> - `php_input`: the PHP runtime and pool of Instance 42
  %%> - `runtime_definitions`: its Process and Schedule definitions
  %%> - the account `orbit-app-7` and its home
  %%> Result:
  %%> - deployment 89 recorded as a running rollback; task #5151 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - automatic deployment pauses, and its schedule is removed
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>php_input, runtime_definitions
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run of `operation-instance-rollback` on Swamp serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the release name, `php_input` and `runtime_definitions`
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no GitHub token and no `.env`: a rollback fetches nothing and writes no environment
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - 900 s
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5151
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task until it ends
  SW->>N: Find retained release<br/>@swamp/ssh · read only
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over `@swamp/ssh` from 209, with `command/shell` steps
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the current selection
  %%> - checks again that the release exists under `releases/`, records this repository, and keeps its web root inside it
  %%> Why again:
  %%> - a deploy's cleanup can remove the release after the request; then `rollback.release_invalid`
  SW->>N: Activate release<br/>atomic swap of current
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks each served web root and its `.env` links in the release, and adds a missing link
  %%> - replaces the `current` link with one atomic rename
  %%> Cancel:
  %%> - a cancel before this step stops the rollback; after it, the rollback finishes
  opt Instance serves PHP
    SW->>N: Refresh PHP cache<br/>FPM graceful reload · OPcache
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - converges the dedicated PHP-FPM pool from `php_input`
    %%> - reloads it gracefully, so running requests finish; then resets OPcache and waits for it
    %%> When a restart is needed:
    %%> - only when the pool's runtime itself differs, such as the PHP version
  end
  SW->>N: Restart Processes<br/>restart_on_deploy · reload first
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs `runtime_definitions`, in the `process.create` and `schedule.create` shape
  %%> - for each running Process with `restart_on_deploy`: reload when the Process allows it, else restart
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - Processes without `restart_on_deploy`, and stopped Processes, stay as they are
  %%> - no deploy step, no Git fetch, no database change
  SW->>N: Check the selection<br/>current → target · Processes up
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads `current` back and checks it selects `20261030T101500Z`
  %%> - checks that each restarted Process is active
  alt all steps pass
    N-->>SW: release, commit
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the selected release, its commit, and the restarted Processes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the rollback<br/>block old commit · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - deployment 89 succeeds with the release and its commit
    %%> - the commit it moved away from is blocked for automatic deploys
    %%> - automatic deployment stays paused until `instance:update 42 --auto-deploy=true`
    %%> - task #5151 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - the release is gone, a check or reload fails, SSH fails, or 900 s run out
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed_step, selected release
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    %%> - which release `current` selects now
    Note over GW: Record failed rollback<br/>selection kept · task failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - deployment 89 is marked failed; task #5151 fails
    %%> - the old commit is still blocked, and automatic deployment stays paused
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a failure before activation keeps the old selection
    %%> - a failure after it keeps the rollback release selected
    %%> - Orbit restores no data; you own application recovery
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after a fix; it is a new task and safe to repeat
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5151
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
